      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/04/brazil-presidential-election-lula-flavio-bolsonaro",
      "description": "<p>Lula and Flávio Bolsonaro face off in battle between leftwing incumbent and far-right son of jailed ex-president</p><p>Brazilians are going to the polls in the first round of a highly polarised and high-stakes presidential election that could change not only the direction of Latin America’s largest country but that of the entire region.</p><p>The election on Sunday pits the leftwing president, Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva, who is seeking a fourth non-consecutive term, against the far-right senator Flávio Bolsonaro, an ally of Donald Trump and the son of the former president Jair Bolsonaro, who is serving a 27-year sentence <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/05/jair-bolsonaro-coup-plan-2022-election-brazil-air-force-baptista-junior\">for attempting a coup</a> after his failed 2022 re-election attempt.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/04/brazil-presidential-election-lula-flavio-bolsonaro\">Continue reading...</a>",
